<!--ID=5B95B1CC-2C7B-494F-B746-CF22A0E779B7;Version=1|{"Locales":{"en-US":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]},"en-GB":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]}}}-->
<speak xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2001/10/synthesis"
       xmlns:mstts="http://www.w3.org/2001/mstts"
       xmlns:emo="http://www.w3.org/2009/10/emotionml"
       version="1.0"
       xml:lang="en-GB">
  <voice name="en-GB-OllieMultilingualNeural">
    <prosody rate="-10.25%" pitch="-2.25%">
      Jesus said: a certain man had two sons.<break time="500ms"/>
      Two sons, one father, one household.<break time="1000ms"/>
      And the younger son came to his father with a request.<break time="1800ms"/>

      He said: give me the share of property that will come to me.<break time="500ms"/>
      It was a striking thing to ask.<break time="500ms"/>
      An inheritance is given when a father dies.<break time="1000ms"/>
      To ask for it now was to say: I want what is mine, and I want it without you.<break time="1800ms"/>

      The father divided his property between them.<break time="500ms"/>
      He did not refuse.<break time="500ms"/>
      He let the son have what he asked for.<break time="1000ms"/>
      Love does not hold tightly what must be released.<break time="1800ms"/>

      Not many days later the younger son gathered everything together.<break time="500ms"/>
      He packed it all.<break time="500ms"/>
      He set his face toward a far country.<break time="1000ms"/>
      He did not look back at what he was leaving behind.<break time="1800ms"/>

      In that far country he spent everything.<break time="500ms"/>
      The money moved quickly when there was no thought for tomorrow.<break time="500ms"/>
      He spent recklessly, the story says, on loose living.<break time="1000ms"/>
      And when he had spent everything, it was gone.<break time="1800ms"/>

      All of it.<break time="500ms"/>
      Every coin his father had divided for him.<break time="500ms"/>
      Every last thing he had gathered and carried away.<break time="1000ms"/>
      Gone.<break time="1800ms"/>

      He had gone as far as he could go from his father's house.<break time="500ms"/>
      He had chosen the far country fully.<break time="1000ms"/>
      And now the far country had nothing left to give him.<break time="1800ms"/>
    </prosody>
  </voice>
</speak>
